.TH "CONSTANTSOURCENODE.CONSTANTSOURCENODE" "3JS" "October 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
ConstantSourceNode.ConstantSourceNode \- ConstantSourceNode:
ConstantSourceNode() constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]ConstantSourceNode()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates a new
\f[CR]ConstantSourceNode\f[R] object instance, representing an audio
source which constantly outputs samples whose values are always the
same.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new ConstantSourceNode(context)
new ConstantSourceNode(context, options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]context\f[R]
An \f[CR]AudioContext\f[R] representing the audio context you want the
node to be associated with.
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A \f[CR]ConstantSourceOptions\f[R] dictionary object defining the
properties you want the \f[CR]ConstantSourceNode\f[R] to have:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]offset\f[R]
A floating\-point number specifying the initial value of the
\f[CR]offset\f[R] \f[CR]AudioParam\f[R], which determines the constant
value generated by the source.
The default is 1.0.
The value must be finite.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
In this example, an audio context is created, then a
\f[CR]ConstantSourceNode\f[R] is established with its \f[CR]offset\f[R]
initialized to 0.5.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]let\f[R] audioContext = \f[B]new\f[R] AudioContext();

\f[B]let\f[R] myConstantSource = \f[B]new\f[R] ConstantSourceNode(audioContext, { offset: 0.5 });
.EE
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] The new \f[CR]ConstantSourceNode\f[R] created by the
constructor has a \f[CR]channelCount\f[R] of 2.
.RE
